# FIX-P12-2 — withRetry implementation + access policy dependencies
# Executed: 2026-07-18
# Status: CLOSED

## Root Cause
Design §5 mandated withRetry on all seeder AOSS ops but implementation was bare
signedAossFetch calls. First live deploy would: (1) AOSS data-access policy propagates
~30-60s → seeder's first call 403 → CR fail → rollback; (2) createIndex returns 200
but index not immediately addressable → first chunk PUT 404 → same rollback.
Additionally, seeder trigger lacked dependency on access policies.

## Fix
1. Created `services/iso-kb-seeder/src/aoss-retry.ts`:
   - withRetry: base 500ms × 2 exp backoff, 20% jitter, 45s ceiling, max 12 attempts
   - Per-operation retryable sets:
     * aossWriteOp: retries 403/404/429/5xx (index activation path)
     * aossReadOp: 404 = success (absent), retries 403/429/5xx only
     * aossDeleteOp: 404 = success (absent), retries 403/429/5xx only

2. Updated `services/iso-kb-seeder/src/meta-doc.ts`:
   - readMetaHash: uses aossReadOp (404 = null, not retried)
   - writeMetaDoc: uses aossWriteOp (retries 403/404/429/5xx)

3. Updated `services/iso-kb-seeder/src/bulk-index.ts`:
   - deleteIndexIfExists: uses aossDeleteOp (404 = absent success)
   - createIndex: uses aossWriteOp
   - chunk PUT: uses aossWriteOp per doc

4. CDK `infra/lib/ai-stack.ts`:
   - isoKbSeederTrigger.node.addDependency(isoKbSeederAccessPolicy)
   - isoKbSeederTrigger.node.addDependency(aossDataAccessPolicy)
   - IsoKbSeederAccessPolicy captured in variable for dependency ref

5. Unit tests (`services/iso-kb-seeder/__tests__/aoss-retry.test.ts`, 12 tests):
   - Write path: 403→200, 404→201, 429→200, 500→200, non-retryable 400 fails fast,
     transport error recovery
   - Read path: 404 returned immediately (not retried), 200 immediate, 403 retried
   - Delete path: 404 immediate success, 200 immediate, 403 retried

## Evidence
- tsc --noEmit: exit 0
- vitest run aoss-retry.test.ts: 12 passed (12)
- Full suite: 1080 passed | 3 skipped (101 files), exit 0
- cdk synth --all: exit 0
